description:
Design demo-stack/specs/flows-quality/plans/flow-mcp-design.md, sections 4.6 and 5.8: "A typed tool-call record on the step attempt, complete and size-bounded: server, tool, the two fingerprints, the resolved arguments, outcome, duration, answer size and hash. It is written with the attempt whether the step then succeeds or fails, and records an interrupted call as interrupted."

Not built by the tool-input stack (pre-gate adversary adv-flows-tool-run-938092428.md, P2-2 and P2-5). What exists (flows/runtime/tool_input.py):
- a successful read returns the argument edges and one resolved-input edge of kind tool_answer;
- a read that fails with a typed code after it reached out writes one FLOW_HTTP_OUTBOUND_CALL audit row (no arguments) and no edge, so nothing records what was sent;
- a read that is cancelled (the task is cancelled, the worker lost the run) or fails with an untyped exception writes no audit row at all. The HTTP input read has the same gap (runtime/http_orchestration.py).

Wanted: the typed record on the attempt for every call that went out, failed and interrupted calls included, covered by the debug-evidence redaction and the run purge; and one audit row per call for the interrupted case, for the tool read and the HTTP read alike.
